A||N||13||SHalliday||1st time Fiero owner! Just bought 87 GT and rear side glass is split||||5||
Z||000000||SHalliday||05-26-2000||11:07 AM||||Just purchased an 87 Fiero GT V6 and the rear glass panel on both sides are split. I was told this was caused by heat from the engine compartment and if I replaced the panels they would only split again. <P>Is this true? If so does anyone have a suggestion/solution to this problem?<P>I have always loved Fiero's and now that I have one, I would really like to fix this problem properly. Any Suggestions?<P>Scott Halliday<BR>new owner of 87 Pontiac Fiero GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||MotherGoose||05-26-2000||11:25 AM||||I as well am a fairly new owner of an 87 GT.  Both my sail panels were broke in several places.  Through a little research I found that they are pretty delicate when cold, and walnut and such thing falling off the trees in the fall can do a lot of damage to them.  Or it could be damage from a lawn mower shooting rocks.  <P>If you replace them the heat shouldn't hurt them, because they are plastic when they get hot they become a little more forgiving and less fragile.  Then again I could be talking out of my butt.<P>Goose||||reg||1
Z||000002||iplayazi||05-26-2000||11:25 AM||||Go to <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A>  and take a look at their panels. I doubt its cracked from heat but they have scoops on their panels so heat wouldn't be a factor. I have an 87 GT as well, and my panels have never cracked on me.  Have fun with the car I now I have.||||reg||7
Z||000003||Bruce||05-26-2000||12:26 PM||||I remember a site that had the GT rear side windows for $99 each; the Fiero store has them for much more. A little help here!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||05-26-2000||02:34 PM||||I picked up a pair of reproduction GT sail panels from Doug Kinney at Carlisle.  They look like the originals.<P>The originals just craze from age. Then crack or chip easily. I still have a set of originals in the box, but mine are showing signs of age and it will be replacement time.<P>The decision will be use the originals or the reproduction.<P>I can't locates Doug's website address in the search mode.<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000005||MotherGoose||05-26-2000||03:04 PM||||Fiero Heaven has clear or smoked for $99.  I think I am going to order them for there, its the best deal I have seen.<P>Goose||||reg||1
Z||000007||sluppy123||05-26-2000||05:13 PM||||Here's Doug's (Fiero warehouse) website <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/gtwindows.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/gtwindows.html</A> <P>The windows look and fit great.<P>-Brian||||reg||1
Z||000008||SHalliday||05-26-2000||05:34 PM||||Thanks to everyone for the helpful feedback. I think I'll order a set of repo instead of factory originals. <P>Since I posted the original post, I again spoke with the gentleman who sold me the Fiero. He told me that he has noticed a number of Fiero's with the back side glass (sails) with the rear section cut out and left open. If he had kept the car he had planned to do this because it would provide additional cooling for the engine. Has anyone ever heard of this and is it recommended? ||||reg||5
Z||000009||RiceCooker||05-26-2000||05:45 PM||||Correct me if I'm wrong anyone, but the decklid vents are used for hot engine air to escape and forcing air down them would not improve the situation at all. The Sail panels with the scoops are purely cosmetic.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||05-26-2000||07:15 PM||||Am I the only one who has never had overheating problems with a GT.  Since having a Borla exhaust system put on my 87 last fall my running temp seems to be 170 which is lower than what it ran last year. I even put in a new 195 thermostat, thinking that the old one (the original) was stuck open.  I have had the system drained and flushed every couple of years.<P>Being stuck in traffic, the temperature climbs, but then the fan kicks on, just like it is supposed to,||||reg||1
Z||000011||AL||05-26-2000||08:19 PM||||i would buy them from doug, i bought one <BR>from doug got it in 3 days and they look <BR>great, try him you can't go wrong.||||reg||14
Z||000012||Sage||05-26-2000||08:43 PM||||Get them from Doug Kinney at the Fiero warehouse.  They look great, fit right and are made of material superior to the originals.  He has the best price of anyone I know handling them, and is a pleasure to do business with.  Sluppy123 has supplied the contact address.  Just my 2 cents.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000013||Ed||05-26-2000||08:50 PM||||Old Lar: I've had my '87 GT for ten years.  It has NEVER overheated in that time, even in 100 degree + California summers.  If it is hot enough to overheat, it is hot enough to turn on the A/C which turns on the radiator fan and the temp goes right down from the gauge's midpoint.  <P>SHalliday: My side glass (plastic) is original, no rips and only very slight cosmetic discoloration.||||reg||1
Z||000014||2birds||05-27-2000||05:04 PM||||Mine has never overheated.  The only time I've ever seen temps go up abnormally was when I was in the mountains on the Montanabahn, if I had to drop back into 4th gear to go uphill.  Sits right in the middle as long as I'm moving.  My AC is removed, but the electric fan still works the same, if I get stuck in a jam.||||reg||1
